"""Single-stroke plotter fonts (Drawscape-style) for title labels.

Faces:
- futural (default): EMSL Futura-light simplex, full ASCII 33-126
  incl. lowercase — the Drawscape default.
- futuram: EMSL Futura-medium (doubled strokes), same coverage.
- simplex: compact caps/digits/punct face (A-Z 0-9 space + 18 marks).

Coordinates are y-DOWN font units, usable as-is in SVG space.
Advance is precomputed per glyph (futural/futuram follow the reference
renderer: advance = o * 1.68; simplex advance = right - left).
Shape: FACES[name] = {'cap_height', 'space_advance', 'glyphs':
  {char: {'advance', 'lines': [[(x, y), ...], ...]}}}.

ATTRIBUTION (both sources are permissive, spec §7-safe):
- Hershey Fonts originally created by Dr. A. V. Hershey at the U.S.
  National Bureau of Standards (required acknowledgement, Usenet Font
  Consortium distribution).
- simplex JSON organization: Stewart C. Russell's python-hershey
  (https://github.com/scruss/python-hershey, CC0/WTFPL).
- futural/futuram data: techninja/hersheytextjs port of the EMSL
  Hershey engraving fonts (https://github.com/techninja/hersheytextjs,
  MIT Copyright (c) 2014 James T.).
"""

